plan.rationale:
In commit 841816a8c ('mmu: preserve global TLB entries on an ASID-scoped sfence.vma'), Wally introduced ASID-scoped TLB invalidation filtering to preserve global (G=1) page translations when an sfence is scoped to a specific ASID. The commit message explicitly notes: 'Decode sfencevmaAllM (an sfence.vma, sinval.vma, sfence.w.inval or sfence.inval.ir whose rs2 field is x0) and plumb it as TLBFlushAll...'. However, two compounding functional defects were introduced in the implementation of the Svinval extension:

1. Privileged Decoder Defect (src/privileged/privdec.sv line 86):
   The decoder computes:
     assign sfencevmaAllM = sfencevmaM & ~|InstrM[24:20];
   The author assumed that InstrM[24:20] corresponds to register field rs2 for all four instructions. However, under the RISC-V Svinval specification, sfence.inval.ir has funct12 = 12'b000110000001 (0x181), funct3 = 3'b000, opcode = 7'b1110011. It has NO rs2 operand! Bit 20 is bit 0 of the 12-bit funct12 field that distinguishes sfence.inval.ir (0x181) from sfence.w.inval (0x180). Because InstrM[20] is 1, ~|InstrM[24:20] unconditionally evaluates to 0. Consequently, sfencevmaAllM is 0 whenever sfence.inval.ir executes. In src/mmu/tlb/tlbcamline.sv line 116, the line flush logic evaluates:
     assign ShouldFlush = TLBFlush & (~PTE_G | TLBFlushAll);
   Because TLBFlushAll is 0, ShouldFlush evaluates to TLBFlush & ~PTE_G. Any global translation (PTE_G == 1) in the instruction TLB (ITLB) or data TLB (DTLB) is completely ignored and survives the fence intact!

2. Pipeline Flush and PC Redirect Omission (src/ieu/controller.sv line 353):
   In src/ieu/controller.sv lines 353-354:
     assign SFenceVmaD = PrivilegedD & (InstrD[31:25] == 7'b0001001);
     assign FenceD = SFenceVmaD | FenceXD;
   SFenceVmaD only decodes sfence.vma (funct7 7'b0001001). It completely omits sinval.vma (7'b0001011), sfence.w.inval (7'b0001100), and sfence.inval.ir (7'b0001100). As a result, FenceD, FenceE, FenceM, and CSRWriteFenceM = CSRWriteM | FenceM are never asserted for any Svinval instruction. In src/hazard/hazard.sv, FlushDCause, FlushECause, and FlushMCause never fire, and in src/ifu/ifu.sv line 366, pcmux2 never redirects instruction fetch to NextValidPCE. Consequently, instructions prefetched into the pipeline before the fence execute to completion without being flushed and refetched.

This violates the RISC-V Privileged Architecture Specification (v20211203) Chapter on Svinval Extension, which mandates that SFENCE.INVAL.IR synchronizes all subsequent instruction fetches with preceding page table modifications across all address spaces, including global translations.
